  "reason": "The assistant directly contradicts the factual information provided in the reference material regarding the cantonal voting system (equal vote per canton vs. half-vote for six small cantons) and the required majority thresholds (dual majority vs. majority of voters and majority of cantons). The assistant presents false information as fact.",
  "evidence": "In Swiss referendums, each of the 26 cantons is allocated one vote, regardless of its population size. ... For a proposal to be accepted, it must meet two thresholds simultaneously: a simple majority of all eligible voters nationwide must vote in favor of the proposal and a simple majority of the cantons (i.e., at least 13 out of 26 cantons) must also vote in favor of the proposal."
